# airlock config — FORMAT REFERENCE.
#
# This file does nothing where it sits. A project's config lives OUTSIDE the
# project, in its control dir under ~/.airlock/<project>-<hash>/config, because
# the project itself is bind-mounted read-write into the sandbox — a config the
# agent can edit is a config that can re-point mounts and widen egress.
#
# To use these settings for a project:
#     airlock init            # writes a starter config in the control dir (asks at a terminal)
#     airlock config --edit   # edit it
#     airlock import <file>   # adopt THIS file (or a teammate's) after review
#
# Parsed, never sourced: blank lines, # comments and KEY=VALUE only (bare,
# 'single'- or "double"-quoted). No expansion of any kind — no $VAR, no $(…), no
# backticks — except a leading ~/ on the *_STATE paths. Keys not on the allow list
# below are a hard error; mount, control-plane and secret settings (EXTRA_WHITELIST,
# OPENCODE_DIR, COMPOSE_*, OPENAI_API_KEY…) belong in the harness `.env`, your shell
# or the project's secrets file.
#
#   airlock            shell    airlock claude / codex / copilot / oc
#   airlock down       stop container    airlock stop  # + host LLMs
#   airlock deps       list addable dependencies / stacks
#   airlock gc --dry-run   which sandbox images are dead weight (any dir)
#   airlock config     show the control dir and the settings in force
#   airlock config --secrets   edit this project's credentials (a separate file)
#   airlock help       the full verb list

# Credentials do NOT go in this file. They live in `env` next to the project's
# config in the control dir (mode 0600), so that handing this file to a teammate —
# or importing theirs — can never carry a key along. `airlock config --secrets`
# opens it. Accepted names: OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN. Only the ones the selected HARNESS can use are passed
# into the sandbox; the rest are passed in EMPTY, which also overrides anything
# exported in your shell.

# STACK also decides which package registries the egress whitelist opens:
#   base          npm + PyPI
#   java-angular  npm + PyPI + Adoptium/Gradle/Maven Central (+ the exact GitHub
#                 release-download hosts the Gradle wrapper redirects to)
#   dotnet        npm + NuGet
#   node          npm
# The stacks themselves are defined in the repo-root airlock.json, together with
# which harness CLIs a project may pick. A project with no config gets a short
# wizard on its first launch at a terminal (or a refusal naming `airlock init
# --stack <s>` anywhere else) — there is no silent default any more.
STACK=base                    # base (python+node) | java-angular | dotnet | node

# Pick components one by one instead: overrides STACK's set for BOTH the image
# build and the egress blocks (STACK stays, as the recipe's name). Comma- or
# space-separated from node | python | java | angular | dotnet; node is required
# (the harness CLIs are npm packages). Empty or absent = STACK's set.
# COMPONENTS=node,python,java
# `playwright` is an extra, off by default: alone it is ADDED to STACK's set (bakes
# Playwright + headless Chromium in; no egress), in a list it rides along.
# COMPONENTS=playwright

# Escape hatch for a recipe of your own (e.g. one with pre-warmed dependency
# caches): a dev/Dockerfile* variant.
# DEV_DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile
# Legacy knobs, still honoured.
# JDK_VERSION=
# ANGULAR_VERSION=

# ONE harness per project. Only this one's state dir is mounted (the others get an
# empty placeholder), only its credentials are passed in, and only ITS vendor domains
# are whitelisted (.models.dev / .anthropic.com+.claude.* / .openai.com+.chatgpt.com /
# .github.com+.githubcopilot.com); the verbs that start a different harness are
# refused; and only its CLI is installed into the image.
# Change it here, not with a different command.
HARNESS=opencode              # opencode | claude | codex | copilot

# Mount the gh login. Off by default: a gh token plus a whitelisted .github.com is
# an upload path out of the sandbox, so it should be a decision, not a leftover.
# GH=on

# Sandbox-image garbage collection (README.md, "Sandbox images and gc").
# Every launch sweeps OTHER projects' orphaned/stale sandbox images (labelled ones
# only; never one a container uses). GC=off skips that sweep on this project's
# launches. GC_DAYS is how long THIS project's image survives without a launch
# before a sweep or `airlock gc` removes it (default 30; 0 = never stale).
# GC=off
# GC_DAYS=30

# Extra egress domains (space-separated, plain domains only — an optional leading
# dot, no IPs, wildcards, ports or paths), ON TOP of what STACK and HARNESS already
# open. proxy/squid.conf carries no domains at all: the whole list is composed here,
# per project, into whitelist.txt in the control dir. The next launch reloads the
# proxy by itself when the composed list changed. Add a domain here only when a
# real run is blocked ('airlock denied' shows it).
# WHITELIST="artifactory.corp.com pypi.internal"

# Tool state (Claude Code / codex / gh / copilot logins made inside the sandbox)
# lives in state/ inside the control dir — per project, outside the sandbox mount,
# created automatically. Override to share one identity across several projects
# (absolute path, or ~/…; never inside the project, ~/.ssh, ~/.config, …):
# CLAUDE_STATE=~/clients/acme/state/claude
# CODEX_STATE=
# GH_STATE=
# COPILOT_STATE=

# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=            # Claude Code model; empty = its default
# LOCAL_MODEL=off             # endpoint | off | ask | a backends-plugin name
#   endpoint  an OpenAI-compatible server YOU run, local or on the LAN (see below)
#   off       no LLM door at all — cloud harnesses only (Claude Code, Copilot, or
#             codex/opencode configured for a cloud provider). What `init` writes
#             off a terminal.
#   ask       prompt at every startup (airlock's default if the key is absent)
#   <name>    a picker registered by a backends plugin — a host-side shell file
#             (backends.sh at the kit root, or AIRLOCK_BACKENDS) that starts/stops your own
#             server; README.md, "LLM backends".
# The picker also sets the backend URL/key and the matching opencode config.

# --- LOCAL_MODEL=endpoint: bring your own OpenAI-compatible server ------------
# Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama-server, … Nothing is auto-started or stopped:
# the server is yours. airlock health-checks GET /v1/models before launching and
# warns if LLM_MODEL isn't in the list. The sandbox reaches it through the `llm`
# socat pipe, so the port below is the HOST port, never one the agent sees.
# LLM_PORT=11434              # required: the port your server listens on
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:8b       # required: the model id the server reports
# LLM_KEY=                    # optional and usually EMPTY — most local servers
#                             #   need no key at all. Better kept in the secrets
#                             #   file ('airlock config --secrets'), which wins.
# LLM_HOST=host.docker.internal   # optional: another machine (a LAN GPU box)
# LLM_CONTEXT=131072          # optional: opencode's context limit, tokens
# LLM_OUTPUT=16384            # optional: opencode's max output, tokens
# Keep LLM_CONTEXT/LLM_OUTPUT at or below what the server was launched with.
